## Undefined symbols from M15 on (ImplementationPlan.md 5.9.6 'When it runs',
## M15-M19; 5.9.14's texts; 5.10.10). msil-ld binds every undefined symbol
## of the bitcode to the native libraries on its command line (late binding,
## before LTO, by name), and reports what stays unresolved after LTO
## optimization, on the merged module, as lld/ELF and lld/wasm report
## undefined symbols after LTO:
## - an undefined GLOBAL function or variable is 'undefined symbol: <s>'
##   with '>>> referenced by <file>:(<method>)' lines, at most three, then
##   '>>> referenced <n> more times' (lld's form); a name that LTO's
##   optimizer introduced (printf("hi\n") -> puts) is '>>> referenced by
##   ld-temp.o';
## - a libc or libm function binds only through a native input: without
##   one, puts and sqrt are undefined symbols like any other function (M14's
##   frozen D14 table made them 'public' P/Invokes of "ucrtbase", "libc" and
##   "libm.so.6"; linked text never consults it), and with one they are
##   'assembly' P/Invokes of the library's module (5.10.11);
## - an undefined HIDDEN symbol, data or function, is 'undefined hidden
##   symbol: <s>' and never binds late, not even to a native library that
##   defines it;
## - an undefined WEAK symbol that nothing defines stays null for the
##   backend (resolve-weak.test, native-weak-undef.test);
## - on non-Windows triples an undefined __start_X or __stop_X is neither
##   reported nor bound when a bitcode definition names section X (5.9.6
##   'When it runs', M15-M19: whole-program code generation defines it), not
##   even by a native library that defines the name; for another section it
##   is an ordinary symbol (native data, or undefined), and on Windows it is
##   reported.
## A HIDDEN reference to a symbol defined elsewhere links.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: llvm-as data.ll -o data.o
# RUN: llvm-as hidden-fn.ll -o hidden-fn.o
# RUN: llvm-as hidden-data.ll -o hidden-data.o
# RUN: llvm-as hidden-def.ll -o hidden-def.o
# RUN: llvm-as fn.ll -o fn.o
# RUN: llvm-as imports-win.ll -o imports-win.o
# RUN: llvm-as imports-lnx.ll -o imports-lnx.o
# RUN: llvm-as data-def.ll -o data-def.o
# RUN: llvm-ar rcs libdata.a data-def.o
# RUN: llvm-lib /machine:x64 /def:%S/Inputs/native/ucrt-stdio.def /out:stdio.lib
# RUN: llvm-lib /machine:x64 /def:%S/Inputs/native/ucrt-math.def /out:math.lib
# RUN: llvm-lib /out:ucrt.lib stdio.lib math.lib
# RUN: yaml2obj --docnum=1 %S/Inputs/native/glibc.yaml -o libc.o
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname libc.so.6 --version-script %S/Inputs/native/glibc-libc.map libc.o -o libc.so.6
# RUN: yaml2obj --docnum=2 %S/Inputs/native/glibc.yaml -o libm.o
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname libm.so.6 --version-script %S/Inputs/native/glibc-libm.map libm.o -o libm.so.6
# RUN: llvm-lib /machine:x64 /def:hidden.def /out:hidden.lib

# DEFINE: %{err} = FileCheck %s --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR"

# RUN: not msil-ld --lto-emit-asm data.o -o x.il 2>&1 | %{err} --check-prefix=DATA
# DATA:      {{^}}msil-ld: error: undefined symbol: ext_data{{$}}
# DATA-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced by data.o:(main){{$}}

## lld's limit: three '>>> referenced by <file>:(<method>)' lines, then
## '>>> referenced <n> more times' for the rest (here f3 and the initializer
## of the global ptr, which main reads), at the default -O2 and at -O0. The
## lines follow the order of the merged module (5.9.4: the output depends
## only on the inputs and options).
# RUN: llvm-as many.ll -o many.o
# RUN: not msil-ld --lto-emit-asm many.o -o x.il 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | %{err} --check-prefix=MANY --implicit-check-not=error: --implicit-check-not=">>>"
# RUN: not msil-ld --lto-emit-asm --lto-O0 many.o -o x.il 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | %{err} --check-prefix=MANY --implicit-check-not=error: --implicit-check-not=">>>"
# MANY:      {{^}}msil-ld: error: undefined symbol: ext_data{{$}}
# MANY-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced by many.o:(main){{$}}
# MANY-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced by many.o:(f1){{$}}
# MANY-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced by many.o:(f2){{$}}
# MANY-NEXT: {{^}}>>> referenced 2 more times{{$}}

